diff --git a/roadmap/gameplay.md b/roadmap/gameplay.md
index 61f62ba..5d8663b 100644
--- a/roadmap/gameplay.md
+++ b/roadmap/gameplay.md
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@ Part of [`ROADMAP.md`](../ROADMAP.md). The to-do milestones of this part (M11 Ne
 
 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-11-01 (39): The two sounds `missing.md` listed. Written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run (no new test: both are in `App`; the audio count test `every_name_the_java_plays_exists_and_decodes` is updated). `random.drr`: its call sites are `EntityArrow.onUpdate`, twice: the arrow sticks in a block, and it hurts an entity, both at volume 1.0, pitch `1.2 / (r * 0.2 + 0.9)`. (27) had played `random.bowhit` there, a sound b1.7.3 does not have; `Ev::Bow(_, true)` now plays the index's own `random.drr` (already in the table), the formula is unchanged, and `random.bowhit` is gone: its table entry, `assets/sound/extra/random/bowhit1..4.ogg`, the audio test's key and counts (80 - 6 + 7 * 6 + 1 keys, 194 - 12 + 7 * 12 + 1 files). `random.bow` stays. Water poured in the Nether (`ItemBucket.onItemRightClick`): the 8 `largesmoke` puffs are drawn (`fx.puff`, at the poured cell plus a random offset on each axis, no motion); the fizz now plays where the Java plays it, at the ray's origin (the eye) plus 0.5 on each axis, not at the cell. ponytail: `Fx::puff` is the furnace cart's `largesmoke` (one sprite and size for every smoke); a refused arrow hit still sounds, as before.
+- 2026-11-01 (38): The two bed gaps left open by (35). Written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run (+1 test `chunks::tests::a_chunk_made_while_a_worker_generates_it_is_not_replaced`). Respawn at a far bed: `respawn_pos` now `preload`s the bed chunks first, so dying far from the bed, or in the Nether, respawns at the bed instead of the world spawn, and `tile.bed.notValid` no longer needs a loaded-chunk guard. That needed a fix in `ChunkManager::stream`: a worker's generate result was `insert`ed over a chunk that already existed, which would have swapped a preloaded, populated chunk for raw terrain; a result for a chunk that is already there is now dropped. Nether bed: `use_bed` blows it up where `canRespawnHere` is false (`BlockBed.blockActivated`): the tapped half is removed, then the cell one further along `headBlockToFootBlockMap` if it is a bed too, and a power 5 fiery `explode` goes off at the middle of THAT cell. No sleep, any hour. ponytail: `preload` runs on the render thread (once per death); both bed cells are set to air directly, so no bed item is dropped (the blast would take it anyway).
